window.docContents[126].resolve({"/#Jakarta-Persistence--3___-Entity-Operations--3___6___-Entity-Instance-Lifecycle--3___6___4___-Removal":{"contents":"A managed entity instance becomes removed when it is passed as an argument to the remove() method of EntityManager or when the remove operation cascades from another instance to the managed instance.\n\nLet e be an instance of an entity class. If e is passed as an argument to the remove() method of EntityManager, or if the remove operation is applied to e via cascade:\n\n* if e is a new entity, e itself is ignored by the remove operation;* if e is a managed entity, it is marked as removed and the record represented by e is scheduled for deletion from the database at or before transaction commit as a result of the flush operation specified below in Section 3.6.6;* if e is a removed entity, e itself is ignored by the remove operation; or* if e is a detached entity, an IllegalArgumentException is thrown or a failure occurs later when the flush operation occurs.* If e is new, managed, or removed, the remove operation is also applied to every entity t referenced by a relationship owned by e and annotated with the cascade element value cascade=REMOVE or cascade=ALL or mapped as such by the equivalent XML descriptor element.\n\nThe remove() method does not change the state held by fields of the entity instance itself.\n\n\n\nFormalized SpecificationRemove requires a created instance that is not\ndetached. It changes a managed instance's lifecycle state to removed.\nFor new or already removed instances, it leaves the state unchanged.action Remove (e : entity) {\n  require created e\n  require e_phase e ≠ detached\n  if e_phase e = managed then\n    e_phase e := removed\n}\nThe action does not change the instance's persistent identity. Since\nbelongsToContext includes removed instances, it also preserves context\nmembership.\nThe definition pendingRemoval becomes true when a managed instance is\nremoved; deletion of a database record is outside the model.\n\n\n\n","context":"Jakarta Persistence\u00093. Entity Operations\u00093.6. Entity Instance Lifecycle","header":"3.6.4. Removal","id":"/#Jakarta-Persistence--3___-Entity-Operations--3___6___-Entity-Instance-Lifecycle--3___6___4___-Removal"}});